{
    "background_story": "Matthew was a brilliant and eccentric scientist who had spent his entire career studying the art of incubation. His life's work was dedicated to creating a device that could mimic the perfect conditions for a hatchling to emerge from its egg. After years of trial and error, Matthew finally succeeded in cracking the code. His invention, the 'Eco-Hatcher,' was a revolutionary machine that could simulate the exact temperature, humidity, and vibrations needed for a hatchling to break free from its shell. The first hatchling to emerge from the Eco-Hatcher was a rare and endangered species of bird, which Matthew had been working to save from extinction. As the tiny beak poked out of the shell, Matthew felt an overwhelming sense of pride and wonder, knowing that his creation had given new life to a species on the brink of disappearance.",
